From 984d0be73a7199d8cac9df6f9e09727a30e16fe8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:32:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Load the vocabulary weights straight into the display
 carve-out

With SPARK3_DISPLAY_CARVEOUT_WEIGHTS=1 the worker used to load the embedding
and output head into ordinary memory, copy them into the GB10 display
carve-out and free the originals. On GB10 freed memory stays charged to the
process, so that copy left part of the tables' size on the host for good.

Vocabulary-sized weights are now created in the carve-out when the model is
built, one dumb buffer per weight, so the checkpoint streams straight into
them; the packed BF16 head is then packed where it lies. After loading the
worker only confirms that every vocabulary-sized weight of the served model
is in the carve-out and that no buffer was left behind by a dropped layer.

The DSpark drafter's embedding and head are placeholders the target's
replace after loading; they are now built on the meta device instead of as
full-size tables that were allocated and then dropped.
